= Conclusion <sec:conclusion>

We replaced one member of a planted LLM pricing cartel and varied what its successor inherited. Either inheritance kept the cartel price, but only the predecessor's notes carried enforcement, and that enforcement seldom returned to the cartel price.

The broader point concerns evaluation. A successor's price level does not show whether it would enforce, and its notes show what it was handed, not what it will do. A timed forced cut tests enforcement directly, and in simulation it can be run at any handover before the successor is deployed.
